row(3, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'BUT THE LORD WAS WROTH WITH ME FOR YOUR SAKES AND WOULD NOT HEAR ME; AND THE LORD SAID TO ME: ENOUGH FOR YOU; SPEAK NO MORE TO ME OF THIS MATTER. {HP(3, 26, (("ויתעבר", "יהוה", "בי", "למענכם"), "BUT THE LORD WAS WROTH WITH ME FOR YOUR SAKES — the hitpael\'s nine tokens (Psalm 78\'s three, 89:39, the Proverbs\'); the store glossing the pass-root\'s homograph \'and-cross-over\' beside the verse\'s own \'let me cross\'; \'for your sakes\' four seats (computed)"), (("ולא", "שמע", "אלי"), "and would not hear me — one seat (computed)"), (("ויאמר", "יהוה", "אלי", "רב", "לך"), "and the LORD said to me — the seventh frame — ENOUGH FOR YOU: the singular one seat, the plural\'s eight (1:6 first) turned on Moses (computed)"), (("אל", "תוסף", "דבר", "אלי", "עוד", "בדבר", "הזה"), "speak no more to me of this matter — one seat (computed)"))} → {AP(3, 26, (("והוה", "רגז", "מן", "קדם", "יי", "עלי", "בדילכון"), "AND THERE WAS ANGER FROM BEFORE THE LORD UPON ME for your sakes — as at 1:37 (computed)"), (("ולא", "קביל", "מני"), "and he did not accept from me — \'did not accept\' 1:45 and 3:26 (computed)"), (("סגי", "לך", "לא", "תוסף", "למללא", "קדמי"), "enough for you; speak no more before me — the singular one seat (computed)"))} The Sifrei 29: wroth — filled with wrath, or as a woman with child; \'enough\' three readings; the judges\' example; prayer never withheld.')
row(3, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'GO UP TO THE TOP OF PISGAH AND LIFT UP YOUR EYES WEST, NORTH, SOUTH AND EAST, AND SEE WITH YOUR EYES, FOR YOU SHALL NOT CROSS THIS JORDAN. {HP(3, 27, (("עלה", "ראש", "הפסגה"), "GO UP TO THE TOP OF PISGAH — Numbers 27:12\'s Abarim, 32:49\'s Nebo, 34:1\'s \'Nebo, the top of Pisgah\': the outside row 37:11\'s three names (computed)"), (("ושא", "עיניך", "ימה", "וצפנה", "ותימנה", "ומזרחה"), "AND LIFT UP YOUR EYES WEST, NORTH, SOUTH AND EAST — Genesis 13:14\'s \'lift up your eyes\' to Abram with the four directions in ANOTHER ORDER (north, south, east, west), Genesis 28:14\'s a third (computed)"), (("וראה", "בעיניך"), "and see with your eyes — 3:27 and Ezekiel 44:5 (computed)"), (("כי", "לא", "תעבר", "את", "הירדן", "הזה"), "FOR YOU SHALL NOT CROSS THIS JORDAN — one seat; 31:2 quotes it as the LORD\'s word (computed)"))} → {AP(3, 27, (("סק", "לריש", "רמתא", "וזקוף", "עיניך"), "go up to the top of THE HEIGHT and lift up your eyes — one seat each (computed)"), (("למערבא", "ולצפונא", "ולדרומא", "ולמדינחא"), "to the west and to the north and to the south and to the east"))} The Sifrei 29:5-6: a prayer worth a hundred deeds — \'go up\'; the directions of prayer; the son at the bedroom door — a rope\'s width of fifty cubits refused.')
row(3, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'AND CHARGE JOSHUA AND STRENGTHEN HIM AND ENCOURAGE HIM, FOR HE SHALL CROSS BEFORE THIS PEOPLE AND CAUSE THEM TO INHERIT THE LAND YOU SHALL SEE. {HP(3, 28, (("וצו", "את", "יהושע", "וחזקהו", "ואמצהו"), "AND CHARGE JOSHUA AND STRENGTHEN HIM AND ENCOURAGE HIM — one seat; \'be strong and of good courage\' nine seats (31:7, 23; Joshua 1\'s four; David\'s to Solomon) (computed)"), (("כי", "הוא", "יעבר", "לפני", "העם", "הזה"), "for he shall cross before this people — one seat (computed)"), (("והוא", "ינחיל", "אותם"), "AND HE SHALL CAUSE THEM TO INHERIT — one seat; Joshua 1:6\'s \'you shall cause this people to inherit\' the run; Numbers 27:19-23\'s commissioning told as the charge (computed)"))} → {AP(3, 28, (("ופקד", "ית", "יהושע", "ותקפהי", "ואלמהי"), "and charge Joshua and strengthen him and encourage him — one seat each (computed)"), (("והוא", "יחסן", "יתהון"), "and he shall cause them to inherit — one seat (computed)"))} The Sifrei 29:7-9: charge is urging; if he crosses they cross, if he gives they inherit — Ai\'s thirty-six.')
row(3, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'AND WE DWELT IN THE VALLEY OPPOSITE BETH-PEOR. {HP(3, 29, (("ונשב", "בגיא", "מול", "בית", "פעור"), "AND WE DWELT IN THE VALLEY OPPOSITE BETH-PEOR — one seat; \'opposite Beth-peor\' three: this, 4:46 (the law\'s place-stamp) and 34:6 (MOSES\' GRAVE); Peor twelve seats (computed)"))} → {AP(3, 29, (("ויתבנא", "בחילתא", "לקבל", "בית", "פעור"), "and we dwelt in the valley opposite Beth-peor — \'in the valley\' 3:29, 4:46, 34:6 (computed)"))} The Sifrei 30: what made us dwell in the valley — Peor; yet his right hand receives the penitent.')
